pyELK
=====

pyELK is an independent Apache-2.0 reimplementation informed by the source code,
documentation, and tests of ELK Reasoner 0.6.0 at commit
b8ac5ce83db0704a7359d96aa382891e2f547863.

ELK Reasoner is Copyright 2011-2024 the ELK contributors and is licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. Its repository is https://github.com/liveontologies/elk-reasoner.

The pyELK implementation is newly authored in Python and Rust. It does not contain or embed
ELK Java classes or a Java runtime. Behavioural translations and adaptations include a
frozen immutable IR, deterministic codecs, explicit completeness values, pyowl-core shared
snapshot interoperability, a Python backend, and a Rust accelerator.

The source repository's tests/data/elk-v0.6.0/upstream directory contains unmodified copies
of selected ELK 0.6.0 test resources. The adjacent UPSTREAM.toml, manifest.json, LICENSE.txt,
NOTICE.md, and NOTICE.pyelk files record their original paths, hashes, licence, attribution,
and pyELK-generated additions. Those test resources are excluded from release sdists and
wheels. Development-only Java oracle dependencies and generated Java classes/JARs are also
excluded from every pyELK distribution.

The optional extension's production dependency closure is recorded in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/inventory.toml. Apache-2.0 is selected where available;
the required MIT, BSD-3-Clause, LLVM-exception, and Unicode terms are reproduced
under THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/.

